# 必考词 Unit23
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit23核心高频词汇

{{trial}}{/ˈtraɪəl/}}{n. 审判；试验}}{{The trial lasted for three weeks before a verdict was reached.}}

{{trigger}}{/ˈtrɪɡər/}}{v. 触发；n. 扳机}}{{The crisis triggered a wave of protests across the country.}}

{{triumph}}{/ˈtraɪʌmf/}}{n. 胜利；v. 战胜}}{{The team celebrated their triumph in the championship.}}

{{tropical}}{/ˈtrɒpɪkl/}}{adj. 热带的}}{{The tropical rainforest is home to countless species.}}

{{tuition}}{/tjuːˈɪʃn/}}{n. 学费；教学}}{{University tuition has risen dramatically in recent years.}}

{{ultimate}}{/ˈʌltɪmət/}}{adj. 最终的；根本的}}{{The ultimate goal of the project is to improve public health.}}

{{undergo}}{/ˌʌndərˈɡəʊ/}}{v. 经历；经受}}{{The patient will undergo surgery next week.}}

{{undermine}}{/ˌʌndərˈmaɪn/}}{v. 暗中破坏；削弱}}{{Constant criticism can undermine a person's confidence.}}

{{undertake}}{/ˌʌndərˈteɪk/}}{v. 承担；从事}}{{The company undertook the project despite the risks.}}

{{unemployment}}{/ˌʌnɪmˈplɔɪmənt/}}{n. 失业}}{{Unemployment rates have fallen to their lowest level in years.}}

{{uniform}}{/ˈjuːnɪfɔːrm/}}{n. 制服；adj. 一致的}}{{The students wear school uniforms every day.}}

{{unique}}{/juːˈniːk/}}{adj. 独特的；唯一的}}{{Every individual has unique talents and abilities.}}

{{universal}}{/ˌjuːnɪˈvɜːrsl/}}{adj. 普遍的；全球的}}{{Access to clean water is a universal human right.}}

{{update}}{/ʌpˈdeɪt/}}{v. 更新；n. 最新消息}}{{Please update the report with the latest data.}}

{{upgrade}}{/ʌpˈɡreɪd/}}{v. 升级；n. 升级版}}{{The company decided to upgrade its computer systems.}}

{{uphold}}{/ʌpˈhəʊld/}}{v. 支持；维护}}{{The court upheld the decision of the lower court.}}

{{urban}}{/ˈɜːrbən/}}{adj. 城市的}}{{Urban areas face challenges such as traffic congestion and pollution.}}

{{urge}}{/ɜːrdʒ/}}{v. 催促；n. 强烈欲望}}{{The doctor urged the patient to quit smoking.}}

{{utilize}}{/ˈjuːtɪlaɪz/}}{v. 利用；使用}}{{The company utilizes advanced technology in its production process.}}

{{vague}}{/veɪɡ/}}{adj. 模糊的；不明确的}}{{The instructions were too vague to follow.}}

{{valid}}{/ˈvælɪd/}}{adj. 有效的；合理的}}{{The ticket is valid for three months from the date of purchase.}}

{{vanish}}{/ˈvænɪʃ/}}{v. 消失；灭绝}}{{The species has vanished from the wild due to habitat loss.}}

{{variable}}{/ˈveəriəbl/}}{adj. 可变的；n. 变量}}{{Temperature is a key variable in the experiment.}}

{{vary}}{/ˈveəri/}}{v. 变化；不同}}{{Prices vary depending on the location and season.}}

{{vast}}{/vɑːst/}}{adj. 广阔的；巨大的}}{{The vast desert stretches as far as the eye can see.}}

{{vehicle}}{/ˈviːɪkl/}}{n. 车辆；工具}}{{Electric vehicles are becoming increasingly popular.}}

{{venture}}{/ˈventʃər/}}{n. 冒险事业；v. 冒险}}{{Starting a new business is always a risky venture.}}

{{verdict}}{/ˈvɜːrdɪkt/}}{n. 裁决；判断}}{{The jury delivered a guilty verdict after hours of deliberation.}}

{{verify}}{/ˈverɪfaɪ/}}{v. 核实；证实}}{{Please verify your email address before submitting the form.}}

{{version}}{/ˈvɜːrʒn/}}{n. 版本；说法}}{{The latest version of the software includes several improvements.}}

{{victim}}{/ˈvɪktɪm/}}{n. 受害者；牺牲品}}{{The victims of the earthquake received aid from the government.}}

{{violate}}{/ˈvaɪəleɪt/}}{v. 违反；侵犯}}{{The company violated environmental regulations.}}

{{virtual}}{/ˈvɜːrtʃuəl/}}{adj. 虚拟的；实质上的}}{{Virtual reality technology is used in education and entertainment.}}

{{visible}}{/ˈvɪzəbl/}}{adj. 看得见的；明显的}}{{The results of the policy are already visible.}}

{{vital}}{/ˈvaɪtl/}}{adj. 至关重要的；生命的}}{{Clean air is vital for human health.}}

{{vivid}}{/ˈvɪvɪd/}}{adj. 生动的；鲜明的}}{{She gave a vivid description of the event.}}

{{volume}}{/ˈvɒljuːm/}}{n. 体积；音量；卷}}{{The volume of trade between the two countries has increased.}}

{{voluntary}}{/ˈvɒləntri/}}{adj. 自愿的；志愿的}}{{Participation in the survey is completely voluntary.}}

{{vote}}{/vəʊt/}}{v./n. 投票；表决}}{{All citizens have the right to vote in elections.}}

{{vulnerable}}{/ˈvʌlnərəbl/}}{adj. 脆弱的；易受伤的}}{{Children are particularly vulnerable to the effects of pollution.}}
